# [PATCH v3 2/3] lib: sbi: ISA extension emulation.
# Vendored from https://lore.kernel.org/opensbi/20251227121802.15703-3-b.freisen@gmx.net/
# Author: Benedikt Freisen <b.freisen@gmx.net>
# Series: v3 patch 2/3 "Add trap-based ISA extension emulation"
# Brings RVA23U64-mode Zcb (compressed bit-manip) emulation to OpenSBI's
# illegal-instruction trap handler. Lets the X280 (RVA22-class) boot
# stock RVA23 distros (Ubuntu 25.10/26.04) at the cost of trapping into
# M-mode on each Zcb instruction. See bhx#163.

Add trap-based emulation code or compatibility stubs for the following ISA extensions:
Zicbom, Zicboz, Zicond, Zimop, Zawrs, Zfa, Zfhmin, Zcb, Zcmop, Zba, Zbb, Zbc, Zbs, Supm

Signed-off-by: Benedikt Freisen <b.freisen@gmx.net>
